      "raw_yaml": "identifier: FOODON:03315720\npreferred_term: Soy peptone\nontology_mapping:\n  ontology_id: FOODON:03315720\n  ontology_label: vegetable protein, hydrolyzed\n  ontology_source: FOODON\n  mapping_quality: CLOSE_MATCH\n  evidence:\n  - evidence_type: CURATOR_JUDGMENT\n    source: cbclaw_foodon_promotion\n    notes: Commercial food mixture - FOODON is correct parent ontology. Soy peptone\n      is an enzymatic hydrolysate of soybean protein; mapped to FOODON parent 'vegetable\n      protein, hydrolyzed'. No exact FOODON term for soy peptone. CLOSE_MATCH.\n  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION\n    source: MIM curation (#260)\n    notes: 'Added ''Peptic digest of soybean meal'' as a EXACT_SYNONYM (#260): the\n      USP/compendial descriptor for soy peptone \u2014 the same product the record already\n      lists as `Soybean peptone`, `Peptone from soymeal`, `Soytone` and `Phytone peptone`.\n      Names the manufacturing process rather than a different substance. CultureMech\n      uses this surface form and label_index did not contain it, so the lookup missed.\n      No new record: FOODON:03315720 is this record''s identifier, and in MIM the\n      identifier IS the ontology CURIE, so a second record on it would be a duplicate\n      primary key rather than added coverage.'\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: Soy peptone\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: manual\n- synonym_text: Soybean peptone\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: manual\n- synonym_text: Peptone from soymeal\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: manual\n- synonym_text: Phytone peptone\n  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM\n  source: manual\n- synonym_text: Phytone peptone (BD-BBL)\n  synonym_type: CATALOG_VARIANT\n  source: manual\n- synonym_text: Soytone (BD-Difco) or Phytone peptone (BD-BBL)\n  synonym_type: CATALOG_VARIANT\n  source: manual\n- synonym_text: 'Properties: Undefined component'\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: CultureMech\n- synonym_text: Soytone\n  synonym_type: EXAC